WEBVTT

00:00.470 --> 00:05.400
20th Anniversary Project

00:20.620 --> 00:28.710
Sentou Yousei Yukikaze

00:23.380 --> 00:28.710
Battle Fairy

00:23.380 --> 00:28.710
YUKIKAZE

00:53.720 --> 00:55.520
It's an enormous iceberg!

00:55.520 --> 00:57.750
Aren't you going to go look at it, Jackson-san?

00:57.750 --> 00:58.830
Yes, well...

00:58.920 --> 01:02.490
I forced myself to come down here for research, so I'm very busy.

01:02.490 --> 01:04.760
Research? For your novel?

01:05.190 --> 01:08.330
Nonfiction, actually. I'm still new at this.

01:08.330 --> 01:10.090
I'm about ready to start writing.

01:10.430 --> 01:11.830
That's amazing!

01:11.830 --> 01:13.770
I'll read it when it comes out!

01:15.170 --> 01:17.540
Thanks. You be sure to do that!

01:23.380 --> 01:27.750
<i>Even now, it stands in a corner of the Antarctic.</i>

01:27.750 --> 01:29.810
<i>That enormous column of mist.</i>

01:31.520 --> 01:34.660
<i>It is a hyperspace passage...</i>

01:34.660 --> 01:38.990
<i>...created by an alien race known as the JAM for the invasion of Earth.</i>

01:40.200 --> 01:43.400
<i>It was in a sudden raid 33 years ago...</i>

01:43.400 --> 01:46.740
<i>...that we first learned of their existence.</i>

02:08.890 --> 02:11.400
<i>After many, many battles...</i>

02:11.400 --> 02:15.070
<i>...Mankind succeeded in pushing the JAM back through the passage...</i>

02:15.100 --> 02:17.400
<i>...to a mysterious planet...</i>

02:17.400 --> 02:21.200
<i>...which we named "Fairy."</i>

02:28.710 --> 02:32.210
<i>Now that the JAM are gone from our sight...</i>

02:32.210 --> 02:35.480
<i>...most people have lost interest in them.</i>

02:48.030 --> 02:51.060
<i>But the war still rages on Fairy.</i>

02:51.700 --> 02:54.430
<i>Even now, at this very moment...</i>

03:07.750 --> 03:09.420
<i>Ghoul leader to all units.</i>

03:09.420 --> 03:13.120
<i>Sequence D-6. Penetrating enemy intercept line.</i>

03:13.120 --> 03:15.650
<i>Prep for EW. Set master arm to on.</i>

03:16.500 --> 03:18.630
<i>Witch Watch to Ghoul, Harpy.</i>

03:18.630 --> 03:20.490
<i>Merging with targets. Type 1.</i>

03:20.730 --> 03:22.680
<i>Read three bogeys... Correction, five.</i>

03:22.690 --> 03:24.670
<i>Launching from Bravo 4-2.</i>

03:24.670 --> 03:28.800
<i>Those are decoys. Type 2s approaching from 10-7. Reading six bogeys.</i>

03:28.810 --> 03:31.970
<i>Ghoul leader, roger. Radar contact.</i>

03:31.970 --> 03:33.680
<i>Witch Watch, do you read?</i>

03:33.680 --> 03:36.140
<i>Merging with targets. Copy.</i>

03:37.750 --> 03:41.150
<i>Ghoul squadron will hit the Type 1s. All units, follow me!</i>

03:45.890 --> 03:48.490
<i>Copy. Okay, Ghoul leader.</i>

03:50.360 --> 03:53.640
<i>Targets have dropped boosters. Targets closing.</i>

03:58.300 --> 04:01.950
TFS 66th, 205, 207, come down.

04:02.240 --> 04:05.410
TFS 47th, now penetrating area 27.

04:05.410 --> 04:07.140
Move tanker to Alpha 27.

04:07.140 --> 04:09.440
Alpha 27, roger.

04:12.510 --> 04:17.680
<i>Roger. Ghoul leader, diving and closing range. Angels three.</i>

04:25.920 --> 04:29.100
<i>Ten-Five, copy! Ghoul leader, engaging.</i>

04:29.100 --> 04:32.570
<i>Seeker open, locked on. Fox 2! Fox 2!</i>

04:32.570 --> 04:34.280
<i>Ghoul 3's been hit!</i>

04:36.840 --> 04:38.850
<i>Dammit... You little...!</i>

04:43.380 --> 04:46.080
Good kill!
Good kill! Good kill!

04:44.550 --> 04:47.710
Engaging! Ghoul 4, engaging!
Seeker open!

04:49.150 --> 04:51.140
<i>Behind you! Break!</i>

04:55.120 --> 04:56.970
<i>Break! Break!</i>

05:03.030 --> 05:05.110
<i>Break! Break! Break!</i>

05:06.540 --> 05:09.000
<i>Seeker open! Fox 2! Fox 2!</i>

05:12.810 --> 05:14.740
<i>Good kill! Good kill!</i>

05:19.410 --> 05:21.150
<i>Break! Break!</i>

05:21.150 --> 05:23.720
<i>Ghoul 2, cut fuel! Hit your extinguishers! Ghoul 2!</i>

05:23.720 --> 05:25.970
<i>Ghoul 2, do you read me?! GHOUL 2!</i>

05:45.240 --> 05:47.940
One-third of them were shot down.

05:47.940 --> 05:49.600
Poor bastards...

05:50.590 --> 05:53.910
Looks like the JAM have made themselves even more maneuverable.

05:53.920 --> 05:55.710
Let's head back, Second Lt. Fukai.

05:56.620 --> 05:57.710
Roger.

05:58.880 --> 06:02.250
This is Special Air Force unit 3. Code B-3, Yukikaze.

06:03.560 --> 06:05.760
Data collection, complete.

06:08.330 --> 06:10.930
Cannot confirm any survivors.

06:10.930 --> 06:13.160
Mission, complete. RTB.

06:31.890 --> 06:33.790
Go to hell, Reaper...

06:47.440 --> 06:48.400
What's that?

06:48.400 --> 06:50.680
Unknown... Wait, I've got it.

06:50.770 --> 06:55.540
Coming in head on, vector two-niner. We'll cross paths in 120 seconds.

06:57.170 --> 07:00.080
What's with this guy? He's coming straight at us.

07:00.680 --> 07:02.480
No response on the IFF.

07:02.480 --> 07:04.450
Taking evasive action.

07:06.720 --> 07:10.200
He's climbing. Looking for a fight...? Engaging.

07:12.440 --> 07:14.450
Lieutenant, wait! It might be a friendly.

07:15.400 --> 07:17.520
His IFF may be damaged.

07:18.500 --> 07:19.960
How do you know?

07:26.540 --> 07:27.700
A Super Sylph...

07:29.170 --> 07:31.370
It's the same type of plane as us! It's not an enemy!

07:32.180 --> 07:34.140
Lt. Fukai, you saw it yourself, didn't you?!

07:34.480 --> 07:36.050
That's a Sylph!

07:37.650 --> 07:39.050
Then contact it.

07:39.050 --> 07:42.220
I'm trying. No response. Comm channels are closed.

07:44.960 --> 07:46.900
Then it's an enemy.

07:47.700 --> 07:49.230
Lieutenant, stop!

07:49.230 --> 07:51.500
Do you understand what you're doing?!

07:54.500 --> 07:55.910
Yukikaze says...

07:56.870 --> 07:58.330
...it's an enemy.

08:46.090 --> 08:48.990
<i>Runway 2-3, closed for emergency.</i>

08:49.070 --> 08:51.430
<i>FSQ, 4 point 2-1, clear.</i>

08:51.430 --> 08:53.190
<i>4 point 2-1, clear.</i>

08:57.600 --> 08:59.510
Hey! Rei!

08:59.970 --> 09:01.540
Get a medic!

09:01.540 --> 09:03.270
We need a stretcher here!

09:03.270 --> 09:05.060
Get him down from there! Give us a hand!

09:06.980 --> 09:08.060
What were you...?

09:22.360 --> 09:25.990
This is video of the unknown craft B-3 recorded.

09:26.560 --> 09:29.770
That's clearly an Earth Super Sylph.

09:29.770 --> 09:31.700
Alike in every way.

09:31.700 --> 09:35.470
We haven't been able to find the wreckage of the unknown, right?

09:35.470 --> 09:40.300
No reports of deserters or any missing planes or pilots, either.

09:40.610 --> 09:43.950
So then, what is this?

09:43.950 --> 09:45.980
May I?

09:46.150 --> 09:48.580
Be my guest, Colonel Rombart-san.

09:48.580 --> 09:50.090
Thank you.

09:50.390 --> 09:54.200
According to the records, you made visual contact, then engaged.

09:54.480 --> 09:59.990
Didn't you consider that this might be a friendly unit, Lt. Fukai?

10:03.060 --> 10:06.060
I fired because he told me to fire.

10:07.400 --> 10:09.730
If Yukikaze says it's a JAM...

10:10.570 --> 10:13.840
...then it's a JAM.

10:35.130 --> 10:37.500
Did you see their faces?

10:37.500 --> 10:41.820
What you said must have been at least partly right.

10:43.100 --> 10:47.830
Be patient. Being grounded isn't the end of the world. I'll make sure you stay busy.

10:50.150 --> 10:52.290
That'll keep your mind off of this.

11:02.160 --> 11:04.250
See you.

12:56.350 --> 13:05.710
<i>B-7, Control Tower Fairy here. Authorized to land. Wind 190, runway 22. Proceed.</i>

13:06.310 --> 13:11.650
<i>Roger. Ready for landing. Track at the hearing checked.</i>

13:11.660 --> 13:20.890
<i>B-7, Control Tower Fairy here. Authorized to land. Runway 22, Wind 190.</i>

13:21.930 --> 13:25.970
I thought I could have a easier life here on the ground.

13:25.970 --> 13:28.490
But it's far from easy...

13:29.840 --> 13:33.710
Come with me. You need a little party time.

13:44.350 --> 13:48.990
When I first met you...

13:48.990 --> 13:52.890
...you were eating your peas and peaches mixed together.

13:54.360 --> 13:57.890
I thought the way you ate irritated the hell out of me.

13:59.200 --> 14:05.830
I hoped to God you wouldn't be assigned to my squadron.

14:09.070 --> 14:14.080
"That's not an expression you should make while eating", I thought.

14:25.550 --> 14:30.020
<i>You couldn't even tell if it tasted good or bad, could you?</i>

14:34.670 --> 14:39.730
I've always wondered what you were thinking about then.

14:44.580 --> 14:46.710
I don't remember.

14:46.710 --> 14:50.820
Figured you'd say that... Let's go.

15:01.530 --> 15:05.560
Didn't I tell you? We're celebrating your full recovery.

15:18.980 --> 15:21.640
Gonna have to write a report for that, Jack.

15:22.320 --> 15:27.190
You think I could do this job if I was scared of writing reports?

15:29.660 --> 15:32.150
What's so funny?

17:04.150 --> 17:06.450
An unmanned plane?

17:06.460 --> 17:07.530
Yes.

17:08.590 --> 17:12.030
We'll be using the FRX-99 prototype.

17:13.260 --> 17:16.010
We begin practical trials on it next week.

17:17.200 --> 17:21.860
If all goes well, the SAF will become our first unmanned unit.

17:22.640 --> 17:25.270
I'll make preparations to receive it.

17:25.270 --> 17:27.210
One more thing...

17:31.480 --> 17:34.780
Second Lt. Fukai has been promoted to first lieutenant.

17:36.450 --> 17:40.480
The inquiry didn't yield an indictment, so it all worked out well, didn't it?

17:43.020 --> 17:45.960
You don't seem as glad as I expected you'd be.

17:47.860 --> 17:50.130
I'm... glad.

17:50.300 --> 17:53.730
It's because you're going to lose him to Yukikaze again, isn't it?

18:02.810 --> 18:05.720
This is Second Lieutenant Burgadish, your replacement.

18:07.120 --> 18:10.440
This is First Lieutenant Fukai, the pilot.

18:11.120 --> 18:14.160
You flew a Super Sylph in the strategic recon wing?

18:14.160 --> 18:17.450
Just a Type-D with a ramjet booster. But, in the SAF...

18:21.300 --> 18:22.200
Hey!

18:43.860 --> 18:46.580
That's unit 3, which you'll be flying.

18:54.230 --> 18:57.030
Its personal name is Yukikaze.

19:00.100 --> 19:02.200
It's a good name.

19:02.200 --> 19:05.970
Yeah... A good name.

19:19.590 --> 19:21.260
<i>Valac 4 to Valac leader.</i>

19:21.260 --> 19:23.060
<i>Report. Bogeys at 7 o'clock.</i>

19:23.060 --> 19:25.960
<i>Valac leader to Kraken leader. Requesting support.</i>

19:25.960 --> 19:27.570
<i>Kraken leader, roger.</i>

19:27.830 --> 19:29.660
<i>Kraken leader to all units.</i>

19:29.660 --> 19:32.570
<i>Engage bogeys approaching at 11 o'clock.</i>

19:32.570 --> 19:34.520
<i>Valac leader to all units.</i>

19:39.210 --> 19:41.180
Merging on long-range radar.

19:42.840 --> 19:45.980
High-speed heat sources! They're closing on the 42nd!

19:45.980 --> 19:48.280
Damn, they're fast! Are they JAM?

19:48.280 --> 19:50.850
Activate the TARPS. Tell them to evade!

19:50.850 --> 19:51.480
Roger.

19:53.520 --> 19:57.060
<i>This is B-3. 42nd, emergency withdrawal!</i>

19:57.060 --> 19:59.760
<i>PAN, PAN, PAN! Code U!</i>

19:59.760 --> 20:01.750
<i>Uniform! Uniform!</i>

20:03.400 --> 20:04.590
They won't make it...

20:05.500 --> 20:08.130
<i>JAM antiaircraft missiles?! All units, come around!</i>

20:08.430 --> 20:10.100
<i>Pull out! Emergency withdrawal!</i>

20:17.080 --> 20:19.380
They... They're all gone...

20:21.250 --> 20:22.880
A signal?

20:23.320 --> 20:25.360
The air formation data link...?

20:26.230 --> 20:28.160
Stop it, Yukikaze!

20:28.320 --> 20:31.690
Is it ECM? Something using the data link frequency.

20:31.690 --> 20:35.130
Unknown at 3 o'clock! No IFF response!

20:35.130 --> 20:37.400
Is it the Super Sylph we heard about?

20:37.400 --> 20:38.470
There it is.

20:38.660 --> 20:40.230
The JAM!

20:44.510 --> 20:46.170
Let's go!

21:02.990 --> 21:05.070
Lieutenant, don't go in too deep!

21:05.490 --> 21:07.720
This bastard... He's begging me to follow!

21:41.520 --> 21:46.070
ECM! No, it's an interrupt. It's searching our systems!

21:47.000 --> 21:50.170
Activate DOS! Expand substructure!

21:50.170 --> 21:54.570
Roger. Shifting main body to under decoy.

22:14.030 --> 22:15.790
It vanished!

22:16.260 --> 22:18.560
High-speed heat sources at 6 o'clock!

22:19.370 --> 22:20.980
More missiles, moving fast!

22:28.340 --> 22:29.910
Incoming, on our six!

22:56.560 --> 22:59.100
Second wave, inbound! Evasive!

23:08.320 --> 23:10.570
2 seconds to contact!

24:11.510 --> 24:13.500
Returning to base...

24:36.970 --> 24:38.910
Still at it?

24:45.680 --> 24:49.800
There are some answers you can't find no matter how hard you look.

24:50.350 --> 24:52.800
Do you understand what I'm saying?

24:54.290 --> 24:57.960
No one knows what the JAM are really like.

24:57.960 --> 25:00.530
They may as well be monsters.

25:00.530 --> 25:02.030
And this plane...

25:02.030 --> 25:06.990
It may be turning into a monster you can't control.

25:08.600 --> 25:12.530
Mankind's role in this drama may be at an end.

25:44.770 --> 25:46.570
An unmanned plane?

25:47.980 --> 25:50.480
In a war with monsters...

25:50.480 --> 25:52.970
...Man has no chance.

25:55.280 --> 25:57.880
Is that your answer, Jack?!

25:59.450 --> 26:01.260
Yes.

26:01.260 --> 26:06.090
The time has come to leave Yukikaze, Rei.

26:09.700 --> 26:12.190
If you want to cut me loose, just say it!

26:12.300 --> 26:17.240
Cut you loose...?! Have I ever said anything like that?!

26:17.240 --> 26:19.840
After all we've been through...

26:21.940 --> 26:23.100
This is all I have!

26:23.280 --> 26:25.350
We can't beat the JAM with it!

26:25.580 --> 26:27.670
THIS IS ALL I HAVE!!!

26:32.520 --> 26:35.290
There's nothing left for me, either.

26:35.310 --> 26:39.860
Or maybe you think this battle here is meaningless?

26:44.170 --> 26:46.270
That's right, Major.

26:46.270 --> 26:48.670
It's none of my concern.

26:54.380 --> 26:57.610
Major, they're asking for a revision on that budget draft.

26:58.710 --> 27:01.450
See you, Major. We'll pick this up later.

27:01.450 --> 27:03.380
Don't forget that report.

27:03.850 --> 27:06.120
Did the Central Computer come up with this?

27:06.280 --> 27:10.450
Why should the water tower electric bill come out of our budget?

27:10.790 --> 27:12.820
Don't ask me, sir.

27:13.560 --> 27:18.070
Major, we need a final okay on this flight plan.

27:21.770 --> 27:23.970
For this operation...

27:23.970 --> 27:27.630
No changes. Same as usual.

27:28.880 --> 27:32.330
Come back in one piece. That's an order.

27:36.450 --> 27:38.650
So formal, now...

28:04.280 --> 28:05.870
Yeah, Bukhar here.

28:06.780 --> 28:08.650
Is there a problem there...?

28:09.910 --> 28:13.980
Yes, that's how we're going to handle it. Right. Right.

28:32.210 --> 28:35.680
The FRX test...? Yeah.

28:35.680 --> 28:37.970
The flight plan's already set.

29:30.260 --> 29:31.560
Uh, no. I'm listening.

29:41.410 --> 29:44.040
I was looking for something...

29:44.040 --> 29:47.130
Everything... is just fine.

29:48.480 --> 29:50.850
No problems.

30:13.640 --> 30:15.120
Oh, excuse me.

30:16.710 --> 30:18.780
What's going on here?!

30:18.780 --> 30:22.440
We lost B-3 in the vicinity of Sugar Rock.

30:23.580 --> 30:26.420
We lost them on ARSR and SSR.

30:26.420 --> 30:29.680
PR and comm signals have also ceased.

30:30.820 --> 30:33.320
Check for them again!

30:33.890 --> 30:36.890
I've already tried four times, sir...

30:37.930 --> 30:39.100
Then do it again!

30:39.100 --> 30:40.620
Yes, sir!

31:06.590 --> 31:08.690
Why can't we find them?

31:10.160 --> 31:12.960
They must have been shot down...

31:13.230 --> 31:15.490
Think twice before you say stuff like that!

31:15.970 --> 31:17.830
S- Sorry, sir.

31:19.240 --> 31:23.080
Hey! I didn't order that tanker to return yet!

31:23.080 --> 31:24.380
They're low on fuel, sir.

31:24.380 --> 31:26.210
Okay, then request an air search!

31:26.210 --> 31:27.780
Y- Yes, sir!

31:27.780 --> 31:32.120
Hold it! What do you mean you can't send out an air rescue team?!

31:32.890 --> 31:36.360
If we waste more time, we may never find them!

31:36.360 --> 31:37.790
To hell with you!

31:42.160 --> 31:44.320
I can't just give up!

31:45.370 --> 31:48.030
Get every SAF fighter we have into the air!

31:48.270 --> 31:51.510
We... We can't do that without clearance from the commander, sir...

31:51.530 --> 31:55.260
Shut up and scramble them! Call everyone out on this!

31:55.270 --> 31:58.050
Their INS may be out.

31:58.050 --> 32:01.270
Lights! Turn on every damned light in the base!

32:01.580 --> 32:04.210
They'll be able to see us from a long way off!

32:11.090 --> 32:13.160
Satisfied?

32:13.160 --> 32:16.300
Let me send out a search and rescue team!

32:16.300 --> 32:19.790
One more word and I'll have you court-martialed.

32:20.400 --> 32:24.670
I'll fly it! There are plenty of planes we can spare!

32:25.440 --> 32:27.670
Shall I relieve you of duty right now?

32:32.250 --> 32:34.610
File a report.

32:35.920 --> 32:37.350
Also...

32:37.350 --> 32:40.180
You should drink a hot cup of coffee.

32:53.670 --> 32:56.430
Relax. It's okay...

32:57.200 --> 32:58.870
It's okay.

32:59.840 --> 33:02.310
Don't force yourself.

33:02.310 --> 33:03.970
You want to cry?

33:04.750 --> 33:07.650
It's okay. Go ahead...

33:13.550 --> 33:15.520
Fairy Fever, huh?

33:16.290 --> 33:19.090
You must have caught it in the desert.

33:19.090 --> 33:22.520
I sent word to your base that you guys had to make...

33:22.730 --> 33:25.830
...an emergency landing, but you're all right.

33:25.830 --> 33:28.480
They told us to take care of you.

33:30.340 --> 33:32.270
That's all?

33:33.070 --> 33:35.010
That's all.

33:37.910 --> 33:41.710
First of all, you have to build up your strength again.

33:42.680 --> 33:47.050
We're just a front line base, and we can't offer much...

33:51.290 --> 33:53.990
...but I'll have them make something good for you.

34:05.570 --> 34:08.170
<i>Hello? What extension, please?</i>

34:09.140 --> 34:12.850
<i>Hello? Hello? What extension are you... -</i>

34:12.850 --> 34:15.690
No... Forget it.

34:19.590 --> 34:21.180
I know...

34:47.210 --> 34:50.880
You'll be fine now. You don't need to suffer anymore.

34:53.690 --> 34:56.380
I won't let you suffer anymore...

35:01.960 --> 35:03.990
I have some bad news.

35:09.040 --> 35:14.250
Your partner didn't make it.

35:17.310 --> 35:21.480
He paid a high price to save you.

35:23.680 --> 35:28.590
Don't waste his sacrifice. You owe him that.

35:34.430 --> 35:39.370
I'd like to discuss the plane you two were piloting.

35:45.510 --> 35:49.870
You can't return to base unless we repair it, right?

36:09.160 --> 36:13.700
We've been having a hard time working on that complicated electronics system it has.

36:13.700 --> 36:17.730
I'd like you to tell me the security system cancellation code.

36:22.180 --> 36:25.210
There's nothing to be afraid of.

36:25.210 --> 36:28.700
Once it's repaired, you can go home.

36:34.420 --> 36:36.580
Current altitude: 9000.

36:37.990 --> 36:39.690
Data link, looking good.

36:40.230 --> 36:43.150
500 miles to test area.

36:56.910 --> 36:59.790
It really is an amazing plane.

37:00.080 --> 37:03.750
What we don't understand, though...

37:03.750 --> 37:08.810
...is why you chose this roundabout system.

37:09.520 --> 37:13.910
A more direct setup would be easier to communicate with, right?

37:21.490 --> 37:24.430
Well, enough of that.

37:24.640 --> 37:27.640
Tell me the cancellation code.

37:27.640 --> 37:30.990
It just took one phone call for Jack to believe I was okay...?

37:33.010 --> 37:34.710
Bullshit!

37:34.710 --> 37:36.480
Tell me the cancellation code!

39:57.020 --> 39:58.500
What is it? What's wrong?

39:59.430 --> 40:02.360
I don't know! The data link's been interrupted!

40:07.430 --> 40:08.770
It's accelerating?

40:08.770 --> 40:10.700
It's no use! I can't control it!

40:16.040 --> 40:18.010
What's going on...?

40:38.470 --> 40:40.760
It's all right...

40:59.490 --> 41:01.510
It's better this way...

41:25.090 --> 41:27.910
A huge amount of data is being transferred into the FRX!

41:27.910 --> 41:28.920
Is it the JAM?!

41:28.920 --> 41:32.210
No... I've got the monitor back! Connecting now!

41:34.050 --> 41:36.260
What the hell...?

41:45.830 --> 41:46.900
Yukikaze...

42:47.660 --> 42:52.660
In my dreams, it comes so clearly.

42:54.070 --> 42:59.830
Letting me embrace that day.

43:02.240 --> 43:07.110
I've seen a lot of summers off...

43:08.580 --> 43:14.810
...along the way to now.

43:16.060 --> 43:18.720
Long way to home.

43:18.590 --> 43:22.630
Let's head back right now.

43:22.500 --> 43:28.960
Because I long to see your smile.

43:31.000 --> 43:36.070
That empty room I spent miserable days in...

43:37.680 --> 43:43.750
...while the answer was in my heart.

43:45.920 --> 43:50.950
In the place I hid my treasures...

43:52.190 --> 43:58.420
...was where we exchanged promises.

43:59.770 --> 44:02.370
Long way to home.

44:02.170 --> 44:06.170
Because I love your smile...

44:06.040 --> 44:12.610
...that never changes.

44:14.180 --> 44:16.850
Long way to home.

44:16.720 --> 44:20.680
I'll be going back soon.

44:20.550 --> 44:24.120
I'll walk till dawn...

44:23.990 --> 44:27.090
...back to you.

44:28.760 --> 44:31.860
My sweet home!

44:31.730 --> 44:35.260
I wanna back right now!

44:36.100 --> 44:39.100
My sweet home!

44:39.010 --> 44:42.270
I wanna hold your mind!

44:47.010 --> 44:49.610
Long way to home.

44:49.480 --> 44:53.480
Let's head back right now.

44:53.350 --> 44:59.860
Because I long to see your smile.

45:01.560 --> 45:04.230
Long way to home.

45:04.030 --> 45:07.960
I'll be going back soon.

45:07.830 --> 45:11.570
I'll walk till dawn...

45:11.370 --> 45:15.200
...back to you.

46:24.770 --> 46:28.760
Sentou Yousei Yukikaze

46:31.780 --> 46:33.950
Abandoned by Yukikaze...

46:33.950 --> 46:37.160
...Rei lies badly hurt and unconscious.

46:37.720 --> 46:41.690
In the deep blackness where even Major Bukhar's calls to awaken cannot reach...

46:41.690 --> 46:45.150
...he hears Yukikaze's cries.

46:46.600 --> 46:50.260
Cries of "The JAM are there."
